{
 "about": "A second kind of game built with the same tools: a platform course, side on. Walk up a low ledge; walk onto a wooden platform as far as the barrier at its front and press F: the barrier lifts and the platform carries you ten metres across; pull a lever (F) and a stone gate rises; a strip of lava sends you back to the door unless you blink over it with the E skill; open the chest (F) to win before the clock runs out. Four coins on the way fill a bar. Nine graphs: stage, coin, ferry, lever, chest, lava, hero (character template: the blink), player, and the client skill graph. Prints: HP_READY, HP_GO, HP_COIN and HP_SCORE n, HP_FERRY, HP_LEVER, HP_BURN when the lava is touched (the script walks into it once, is sent back, then blinks over), HP_BLINK, HP_CHEST, HP_VICTORY (or HP_TIME_UP), and HP_AT with the character's x and y every two seconds. Climbing is switched off in the class: with it on, a character pushed against the barrier climbs over it (seen twice). The script does not walk by the clock alone, which passed once and failed once: the barrier stops the character at a known place on the platform, and the lava puts it at a known place before the blink.",
